    "result": "All tests pass! Here's what I fixed:\n\n**Issue 1: Missing named export in governance module**\n- The test expected `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `src/finetune/index.js`, but it was only available in the default export\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` while keeping them in the default export for backward compatibility\n\n**Issue 2: Toxicity metric parameter mismatch**\n- The `toxicityMetric` function was designed to accept `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` passes `(outputs, references)`\n- References were being incorrectly used as banned terms, flagging the outputs as toxic\n- Updated the function signature to accept `references` as the second parameter but always use `defaultBannedTerms` internally, making it work correctly when called from `runEvaluations`\n\nAll 28 tests now pass \u2713",
